From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: subarr-subgen <subarr@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0062: advertise which audio track subgen will transcribe

subarr cannot choose transcribe vs translate per file without knowing which
audio language subgen will actually use. choose_transcribe_language picks it
in this order: the forced language, FORCE_DETECTED_LANGUAGE_TO,
PREFERRED_AUDIO_LANGUAGES in list order against the file's tracks, then the
default track. Only the first was visible to subarr.

Adds two values to the capabilities block served by GET /queue:

- preferred_audio_languages: the list in order, unfiltered, duplicates kept.
  An entry that parsed to LanguageCode.NONE is emitted as null, NOT dropped:
  upstream matches a NONE entry against an untagged track and the falsy
  result makes choose_transcribe_language fall through to the default track,
  skipping every later entry. Dropping nulls would make subarr predict an
  entry subgen never reaches.
- force_detected_language_to: the ISO 639-1 code, or null when unset.

Both are values, not boolean flags, so the capability audit's flag list is
unchanged. Requested by AztecGuyGDL as coaxk/subarr#633.
---
 subgen.py | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subgen.py b/subgen.py
index 4173662..1071c06 100644
--- a/subgen.py
+++ b/subgen.py
@@ -904,6 +904,27 @@ def queue_status():
             # full producible set: English via translate, or the file's own
             # audio language via transcribe.
             "transcribe_or_translate": transcribe_or_translate,
+            # [v4.38 PATCH #633] Which audio track subgen will TRANSCRIBE, as
+            # far as the instance settings decide it. choose_transcribe_language
+            # tries: the forced language, FORCE_DETECTED_LANGUAGE_TO, then
+            # PREFERRED_AUDIO_LANGUAGES in list order against the file's tracks,
+            # then the default track. None of the last three were visible, so
+            # subarr could not tell which audio language a file would be
+            # transcribed from, and so could not pick transcribe vs translate
+            # per file (coaxk/subarr#633, reported by AztecGuyGDL).
+            #
+            # The list is emitted IN ORDER, unfiltered, duplicates kept, and an
+            # entry that parsed to LanguageCode.NONE is emitted as null rather
+            # than dropped. Upstream's find_language_audio_track matches a NONE
+            # entry against an untagged track and returns NONE, which
+            # choose_transcribe_language treats as falsy ("no preferred match"),
+            # so it falls through to the default track and never reaches any
+            # LATER entry. Dropping the nulls would make subarr predict a later
+            # entry that subgen never gets to.
+            "preferred_audio_languages": [
+                (lc.to_iso_639_1() or None) for lc in preferred_audio_languages
+            ],
+            "force_detected_language_to": force_detected_language_to.to_iso_639_1() or None,
             # Renames the OUTPUT FILE without changing the language of its
             # CONTENTS. An install in translate mode with
             # SUBTITLE_LANGUAGE_NAME=es writes English text into a .es.srt,
